corpus and DI2 project lifecycle contracts are reviewed and approved.","evidence":"The only file evidence is `plans/design-intelligence-implementation.md:1`, which shows the header \"# Design intelligence implementation plan\". That proves the plan document exists, but it does not show the DI1/DI2 contracts or any sequencing between them. The grep for `/(?i)approvedAt/` found 0 matches, so nothing shows that the DI1 corpus or DI2 project-lifecycle contracts have been approved. Nothing shows dependent workflow work being held until they are. The evidence neither confirms nor contradicts the ordering claim (anchors c3, c4, c5, k3), so the premise is unverifiable.","action":"Give the ordering a checkable form. Point the premise at the specific section or line of `plans/design-intelligence-implementation.md` that sequences dependent workflow tasks after the DI1/DI2 contracts. Also state the gate that enforces it, for example the DI1/DI2 contract artifacts carrying `approvedAt`, or a task dependency edge in the plan. Then re-run the probes against those anchors. If no such gate exists, record it as a process precondition that the plan states but the code does not enforce.","fixability":"assisted","proposedFix":{"rationale":"The ordering claim cannot be checked against the evidence. No approval stamps were found, and the only read line is the plan's title. Choosing how to ground the premise needs a human decision. Nothing in the evidence supports an automatic text edit.","options":["Cite the exact `plans/design-intelligence-implementation.md:<line>` where dependent workflow tasks are listed after the DI1/DI2 contracts, and re-probe it.","Name the approval artifacts for the DI1 corpus and DI2 lifecycle contracts (paths of the DEF/HLD/LLD files), and make `approvedAt` on those artifacts the gate.","Reword the premise as a stated process precondition that the code does not enforce, which lowers its weight in the review."]}},{"claimId":"p12","ref":"s6/ac1","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"Internal consistency: open question a2 (specimens vs. written guidelines only) is listed as still open in §8 and as a 'low' assumption in §4, yet is recorded as resolved (q1d8128b2: include lightweight palette/typography/component-state/layout examples) — the resolved state must be the one reflected, and S006 ac1 matches the resolution.","evidence":"The only gathered evidence is one grep match for `q1d8128b2`: docs/epics/di3-guideline-creation-revision-agent-reuse-E20261011b452bdbf/DEF.md:167 — \"- `q1d8128b2` — Item a2: Confirm whether the first release includes lightweight palette/type/component/layout specimens or written guidelines only before designing story s6.\" That line shows the question still listed as open. Nothing in the evidence records it as resolved. No match or read shows a resolution record for q1d8128b2, the §4 Assumptions entry for a2 (marked 'low'), or the text of S006 ac1. So the evidence supports half of the premise: a2/q1d8128b2 is still listed as open. It does not support the other half: that a resolution exists (\"include lightweight palette/typography/component-state/layout examples\") and that S006 ac1 matches it. Since the inconsistency cannot be confirmed from the evidence, the premise is unverifiable. This is MED, not HIGH: the decision only affects whether S006 ac1 includes specimens, and no concrete build failure can be named from this evidence.","action":"Check whether DEF.md actually records a resolution for q1d8128b2. If it does, remove a2/q1d8128b2 from §8 Open questions and from the 'low' entries in §4 Assumptions, record the decision (include lightweight palette/typography/component-state/layout specimens), and confirm S006 ac1 says the same. If no resolution exists, keep q1d8128b2 open and make sure S006 ac1 does not settle the question before the user decides, since DEF.md:167 says to confirm it \"before designing story s6\".","fixability":"assisted","proposedFix":{"rationale":"The evidence only shows q1d8128b2 still listed as open at DEF.md:167. The resolution text, the §4 entry and S006 ac1 were not in the evidence, so no find/replace can be built from it safely. A person needs to confirm which state is correct.","options":["The question is resolved (specimens included): move q1d8128b2/a2 out of §8 Open questions and §4 Assumptions into a recorded decision, and keep S006 ac1 as it is.","The question is still open: keep q1d8128b2 in §8, and change S006 ac1 so it does not assume specimens until the question is answered.","The question is resolved as written guidelines only: record that decision and remove the specimen requirement from S006 ac1."]}},{"claimId":"p13","ref":"k2","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"Guideline versions carry an approval state such that approval is explicit and version-specific per UI type, activation is withheld when review is stale/blocking, and current approved sets remain active until a replacement version is approved (k2, S003, S004 ac2).","evidence":"The gathered evidence does not support the premise. `grep /(?i)guideline.*version/` found 0 matches, so nothing in the source tree models a guideline version or an approval state per version. `grep /(?i)stale/` found 0 matches, so nothing models withholding activation when a review is stale or blocking. The only read was `docs/plans/design-intelligence-prd.md:1`, which returned just the heading \"# insrc Design Intelligence PRD\". It does not mention approval states, explicit approval per UI type, stale-review gating, or keeping the current approved set active until a replacement is approved. No match or read line confirms any of the three parts of the premise. The PRD exists, so the premise may come from requirements in its later sections, but those sections were not part of the evidence. The premise is therefore unverifiable, not contradicted.","action":"Ground the premise before building on it. Cite the specific PRD sections (for k2, S003 ac1/ac3, S004 ac2) that set out: (a) explicit approval for each version and each UI type, (b) activation withheld when the review is stale or blocking, and (c) the current approved set staying active until a replacement version is approved. Then re-probe for those terms, such as \"approv\", \"activation\", \"UI type\" and \"replacement\", in docs/plans/design-intelligence-prd.md. If this is greenfield behaviour, state plainly in the artifact that no guideline-version or stale-review model exists in code yet and that the task must create it, rather than implying it is already there.","fixability":"assisted","proposedFix":{"rationale":"The evidence has no matches for guideline versioning or stale-review gating, and only the PRD heading was read, so none of the premise's parts can be checked. The fix is to anchor the premise in the PRD text that supports it, or to mark it as new behaviour. Which applies needs a person to read the PRD sections, so no automatic edit is safe.","options":["Add explicit PRD section and line citations for each part of k2 (version-specific approval per UI type, activation withheld on a stale or blocking review, current set kept until a replacement is approved), then re-run the review probes against those lines.","Rewrite the premise as a greenfield requirement, e.g. 'No guideline-version approval model exists today; S003/S004 introduce version-specific approval state per UI type, stale/blocking-review activation gating, and retain-until-replaced semantics', so the build task creates the model rather than extending one.","Split k2 into three separate premises (explicit approval per version and UI type, the stale/blocking activation gate, retain-until-replaced) so each can be grounded and checked on its own."]}},{"claimId":"p14","ref":"s5","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"Agent consumption of guidelines (S005) is read-only: requesting design context returns and records the active version without creating drafts, approval requests, or silently generating/substituting a missing set.","evidence":"The gathered evidence does not cover this premise. `grep /(?i)active guideline/` found 0 matches in the source tree. The only read, `docs/plans/design-intelligence-prd.md:1`, returned just the document title (`# insrc Design Intelligence PRD`). It contains nothing about S005, FR002, s5/ac1 or s5/ac2, and nothing on read-only guideline consumption, recording the active version, or forbidding drafts, approval requests and silent generation or substitution of a missing set. No code path, handler or acceptance-criteria text was found to confirm or contradict the premise. The premise is therefore UNVERIFIABLE. The evidence does not contradict it, so no concrete build failure can be named and it is not HIGH.","action":"Re-ground the premise. Cite the exact PRD section that defines S005, FR002 and s5/ac1–ac2, using a `path:line` beyond the title line. Re-probe with terms that match the PRD's own wording, for example `guideline`, `S005`, `FR002` or `design context`, instead of the literal phrase \"active guideline\". If the premise names an existing design-context handler or guideline store that must stay read-only, cite its `file:line` so a probe can confirm it has no write, draft or approval side effects. If neither exists yet (greenfield), mark the premise as a forward requirement taken from the PRD, not a claim about current code.","fixability":"assisted","proposedFix":{"rationale":"The evidence neither confirms nor refutes the premise, so no edit can be derived from it. A human needs to supply or confirm the anchor that grounds S005/FR002.","options":["Add a precise anchor: cite the `docs/plans/design-intelligence-prd.md` line range that defines S005 / FR002 / s5/ac1–ac2, and re-run the review with probes such as `S005|FR002|guideline`.","Re-label the premise as a forward PRD requirement (greenfield, with no existing code to verify against) so reviewers do not expect it to be grounded in source code.","If an existing design-context or guideline-read path is involved, add its `file:line` and a probe asserting it makes no draft or approval writes and does no fallback generation."]}},{"claimId":"p15","ref":"k4","kind":"external-contract","severity":"MED","premise":"Cloud LLM reasoning for this workflow runs via the claude/codex CLI subprocess provider (CliProvider), with no direct cloud REST, and provider calls are issued serially.","evidence":"The evidence backs the CliProvider part of the premise. `src/agent/providers/cli-provider.ts:131` declares `export class CliProvider implements LLMProvider`, and `read src/agent/providers/cli-provider.ts:1 → FOUND` shows the anchor file exists. The only other provider class found is `src/agent/providers/ollama.ts:150 export class OllamaProvider implements LLMProvider`, which is local. No cloud REST provider class appears in the matches. Earlier reviewed artifacts (DEF.md:152, HLD.md:462) cite CliProvider at :88, but the current source puts it at :131. The premise names only the file, not a line, so this drift does not affect it. Two parts of the premise are not covered by the evidence: (1) that provider calls are issued serially, and (2) that no direct cloud REST call exists anywhere. The probes only matched class declarations. Nothing was read or searched for `Promise.all` around provider calls, or for `fetch`/`undici` calls to anthropic/openai endpoints. So the serial-call guarantee cannot be verified from this evidence.","action":"Keep the CliProvider part of the premise; the evidence confirms it. Add a probe for the serial-call claim, for example a search for `Promise.all` next to `.complete(`/`.embed(` calls in the workflow's code path. If no probe is added, mark the serial part as a project rule from CLAUDE.md that this evidence does not check. Optionally add a probe for direct cloud REST, such as a search for `api.anthropic.com|api.openai.com` under src/, to back the \"no direct cloud REST\" part. Either way, what gets built does not change.","fixability":"assisted","proposedFix":{"rationale":"The CliProvider routing is verified at cli-provider.ts:131. The serial-call and no-REST parts are not covered by the gathered evidence. They need either an added probe or a rewording that marks them as a project rule, not a verified fact. This is not a design gap: the build is the same either way.","options":["Keep the premise text and add probes: rg `Promise\\.all` near provider `.complete(`/`.embed(` calls, and rg `api\\.anthropic\\.com|api\\.openai\\.com` under src/","Reword so it marks which parts are verified: 'Cloud LLM reasoning runs via CliProvider (src/agent/providers/cli-provider.ts:131); serial provider calls and no direct cloud REST are project rules (CLAUDE.md) that the build must follow.'","Split into two premises: k4a (CliProvider routing, verified) and k4b (serial calls + no REST, project rule, needs its own probe)"]}},{"claimId":"p16","ref":"s6/ac2","kind":"inventory","severity":"MED","premise":"S006 ac2's evaluation uses eight project briefs across three UI types with several representative pages each, reported against the PRD acceptance criteria — the PRD must define those criteria and counts.","evidence":"Only the file's existence is confirmed: `read docs/plans/design-intelligence-prd.md:1` shows the heading \"# insrc Design Intelligence PRD\". Nothing confirms the claim about what the PRD contains:\n- `grep /(?i)eight (project )?briefs/` found 0 matches, so no \"eight briefs\" count was found.\n- `grep /(?i)acceptance criteria/` found 0 matches, so no section titled \"acceptance criteria\" was found.\n- No match supports \"three UI types\" or \"several representative pages each\".\n\nThe PRD exists, but none of the counts or the acceptance-criteria section that s6/ac2 relies on could be found. The evidence also doesn't rule out that the PRD covers this under other wording, such as \"success criteria\" or \"evaluation\", which was not grepped. Because of that I can't state a definite failure in the build, so this is rated unverifiable (MED), not contradicted (HIGH). Still, if the PRD really has no such criteria, the evaluation in s6/ac2 would have nothing to report against.","action":"Search docs/plans/design-intelligence-prd.md for the evaluation section under other wording (success criteria, evaluation, briefs, UI types, pages). If you find it, change the s6/ac2 premise to name the real section heading or `path:line`, and the actual counts of briefs, UI types and pages. If the PRD has no such section, choose one of two fixes: (a) add the evaluation criteria and counts to the PRD (8 briefs, 3 UI types, N pages each) before S006 runs, or (b) restate s6/ac2 so it defines its own pass and fail criteria instead of pointing to PRD criteria that don't exist.","fixability":"assisted","proposedFix":{"rationale":"The evidence confirms the PRD exists but none of the cited content, so there is no evidence-backed value to put in an automatic edit. Someone needs to either find the PRD section under other wording or decide where the criteria should be defined.","options":["Find the PRD's evaluation or success-criteria section under other wording, then rewrite the premise to cite its exact heading or path:line and the real counts.","Add an 'Evaluation acceptance criteria' section to docs/plans/design-intelligence-prd.md that sets 8 briefs, 3 UI types and N representative pages each, plus pass thresholds. Make that a prerequisite of S006.","Rewrite s6/ac2 to state its own measurable criteria (brief count, UI types, pages per type, thresholds) instead of deferring to the PRD."]}}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":14,"low":2},"reviewedAt":"2026-10-11T14:58:28.727Z","model":"cli-claude:opus","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
